An edited .docx carries the change as a tracked revision by its author.

```console
$ stetdoc edit contract.docx -o edited.docx --author "Jane Doe" --ops batch.txt
applied 1 operation, tracked as Jane Doe 2026-10-06T09:30:00Z. base 745747bfd39463c1:0:745747bfd39463c1
0 replace p4: deletion #0, insertion #1
p4 Payment is due within {--thirty--}{#0 JD}{++sixty++}{#1 JD} days.
validated 1 unit: no problems, and this file needs no separate check.
wrote edited.docx

$ stetdoc view edited.docx --range p4..p4
{stet 1 view=body base=745747bfd39463c1:0:745747bfd39463c1 mode=redline common-style="Normal" range=p4..p4}
2 tracked changes by Jane Doe already in the document: #0 delete p4 "thirty", #1 insert p4 "sixty".
If you did not make them, tell the user about them.
{authors: JD "Jane Doe"}
{summary: 2 tracked changes (JD 2) · 1 section}
p4 Payment is due within {--thirty--}{#0 JD}{++sixty++}{#1 JD} days.
{position: p4..p4 of p4..p4 (1 of 1 blocks)}

$ stetdoc view edited.docx --range p4..p4 --mode final
{stet 1 view=body base=745747bfd39463c1:0:745747bfd39463c1 mode=final common-style="Normal" range=p4..p4}
2 tracked changes by Jane Doe already in the document: #0 delete p4 "thirty", #1 insert p4 "sixty".
If you did not make them, tell the user about them.
{summary: 2 tracked changes (JD 2) · 1 section}
p4 Payment is due within sixty days.
{position: p4..p4 of p4..p4 (1 of 1 blocks)}

```
